{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525281-how-do-you-create-npcs","id":1525281,"title":"How do you create NPCs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-09T18:33:43-08:00","id":1525281,"title":"How do you create NPCs?","content":"<br /> We're still playing 2E. My players have visited practically every place that's got a chapter in Terrestrial and Celestial Direction splatbooks - and made a mess of them - because ... Exalted PCs.<br /> <br /> They've taken to picking some blank space on the map for their PCs to explore. I can't really stop them without railroading them because the Sid with Mirror-Shattering Method knows the courses to everywhere except Autotchtonia.<br /> <br /> Not that I would want to.<br /> <br /> My solution has been: a lone DB exalted in a small town there and beat the odds. They're about a century old and have established themselves and their descendants as a local power-that-is.<br /> <br /> I start with a randomly generated name, a 0xp character concept suitable for the direction, an asthetic for the place, and go from there by statting the NPC to 800xp in 100xp decade-long increments. Then I add their exalted descendants to the mix.<br /> <br /> I've got five sets of NPCs with a little blurb describing what's there and ready. Clockwise, from the North, with the scavenger lands last:<br /> <br /> Windhamshire: medieval England c.1250 with an arctic climate. Ruled by Lucille, 1st Earl of Windhamshire<br /> <br /> Compt\u00e9 de Havre: medieval France c.1400 fending off the Raksha. Ruled by Riko, Compte du Havre<br /> <br /> Wanyasi: arid grassland/desert semi-nomadic bands of hunter-gatherers acclimated to excessive heat. Lindiwe is the Elder Chieftan.<br /> <br /> Isola di Mille Miglia: renaissance Venice, Italy ... on an island the middle of nowhere. Barone Ferruccio is the elected Principe of the city-state and Ammiraglio della Flotte.<br /> <br /> Ky\u014d: a feudal Japanese asthetic which values very large families. Mizuki is of Lord of Ky\u014d. Mizuki has 23 living Terrestrial descendants with a lot more on the way. The die rolls say: 59 of her descendants currently under the age of twenty using probabilities <i>less generous</i> than what the 2E Errata and Terrestrial Bloodline Merit call for will exalt before Mizuki's 120th birthday.<br /> <br /> What I started from, including what the name roughly means in modern English:<br /> <br /> Lucille &quot;light&quot; - Air Aspect, Sorcerer<br /> <br /> Rico &quot;white jasmine child&quot; - Earth Aspect, Artificier, Hates Fae<br /> <br /> Lindiwe &quot;awaited, waited for&quot; - Fire Aspect, Southern Chieftian<br /> <br /> Ferruccio &quot;iron, sword&quot; - Water Aspect, Fisherman<br /> <br /> Mizuki &quot;auspicious hope&quot; - Wood Aspect, Illegitimate daughter of a passing Dynast and an innkeeper's wife.<br /> <br /> What I got, when I statted them to 800xp with &quot;this seems like how they'd age&quot; as the guide:<br /> <br /> Lucille: Windhamshire's government is a mashup of the English government c.1215 (the Magna Carta) and c.1689 (the Bill of Rights) without all the intervening internal strife. One of her backgrounds is Retainer:5 Parliament (every elected town mayor). Their Magna Carta Libertatum was sanctified and sealed by the Unconquered Sun (that was a really good no-stunt NPC prayer roll my players gave the thumbs up to).<br /> <br /> Rico: About equal to Tepet Ejava in terms of overall military prowess even though he has no formal military training. He just sorta got that way by default of being the owner of a manse which mortals use for shelter when the jingling bells of the fair folk can be heard in the distance.<br /> <br /> In a melee duel with Ejava (before charms, stunts, and other magic):<br /> - accuracy:15 damage:+11/14L PDV:8 rate:2 - Rico, with his N/A white jade dire lance<br /> - accuracy:10 damage:+10L PDV:5 rate:3 - Ejava, with a jade daiklave<br /> <br /> Rico when there's a hostile-to-Rico Raksha within (essence) miles? Double every dicepool he's got and his Dire Lance now inflicts unsoakable aggravated levels instead of just the standard soakable lethal dice.<br /> <br /> His motivation is &quot;No Fae&quot; and Artifact N/A in the right hands is not a joke.<br /> <br /> Lindiwe: You aren't keeping up with her unless you've got charms or other magic which lets you maintain a feat of endurance for at least 13-hours without a break. That's when she starts rolling (stamina + resistance + specialty) for fatigue in 1B/hour excessive heat she's acclimated to and can ignore.<br /> <br /> Ferrucio: His manse is fire aspected and vents pure sulphur. His 1st wife was a thaumaturge who figured out how make saltpeter from urine. They already knew about charcoal. Isola di Mille Miglia completely ignores things like the &quot;gunpowder does not exist&quot; fantasy gun control authors like to impose on fantasy settings like Exalted. When they say &quot;that was available in Europe c.1600&quot; I'll say &quot;You can have it and use it ...<br /> <br /> ... but you aren't going to like the reload times, crafting times, and maintainence times.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mizuki: A complete repudiation of the canon assertion that DBs are rare special snowflakes thanks to the demographic die rolls indicating that Ky\u014d is going to be majority-DB well before Mizuki's first (stamina + resistance + essence + breeding) - she has breeding:3 and Well-Tended Garden of the Soul - 21-die death-from-old-age roll which will only fail if she botches both the initial roll and the 3m re-roll.<br /> <br /> That roll ain't happening for another 150 years and Mizuki ain't gonna ever botch it because she's got the Thousand-Correct Actions &quot;discount for a specialty&quot; excellency for Survival which gives her a basically free reflexive auto-success on any survival roll when &quot;preparing food&quot; is in play before craft (water:1, (cooking:+3)) even enters the conversation.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T05:53:42-08:00","id":1525306,"title":"","content":"I normally find a character in some media I think might have an interesting dynamic with the PCs, shamelessly steal them and then either pull numbers/tricks out of thin air mid-session or take the time to build them up like full characters (depending on how much use I expect them to see).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T10:40:22-08:00","id":1525315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525281-how-do-you-create-npcs?p=1525306#post1525306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I normally find a character in some media I think might have an interesting dynamic with the PCs, shamelessly steal them and then either pull numbers/tricks out of thin air mid-session or take the time to build them up like full characters (depending on how much use I expect them to see).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good approach.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> My approach to &quot;I need a named NPC <i>right now</i> because that extra just rolled all 10s mid-session&quot; is to throw one of my siblings or their spouse under the bus.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bMy players are my wife and teenage daughters plus my daughter's boyfriends and a nephew. They know who is on &quot;Daddy's fecal roster&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T18:27:59-08:00","id":1525336,"title":"","content":"My approach is kind of overly methodic in that i frequently use NPCs as tools in my worldbuiling, so many of them come to be because i had one or more ideas to explore in how a certain nation, city-state or village was supposed to be.<br /> <br /> All too frequently i would just go over a lot of the antagonist templates in the Corebook or a relevant direction-book and ask myself &quot;how does it fit or not in THIS place? what differences or twists could plot, local culture or intrigues add to make this guy or lady a little more unique?&quot;<br /> <br /> Mortals, beastfolk, wyld mutants, animals - all of those can serve quite well to establish an identity or color to a place visited by a circle of Exalts. It is also a good stage to insert some better than average but still not supernatural individuals like thaumaturgists of all sorts, the occasional terrestrial circle sorcerer or martial artist (or even a whole school of either, if not both) for some bit of oomph &amp; weirdness.<br /> <br /> And do not forget giving the occasional artifact, hearthstone, familiar or other cool beanies too. Things in the 1-3 range can be pretty damn fine as long as you can make them somewhat characterful.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dragon-bloods.... yeah, i also use them some, but just as frequently or more i'll use all sorts of spirits - elementals, deities, demons, ghosts, raksha (or more obscure/homebrewed classes of beings), not to mention their occasional or not so occasional descendants with native populations, human, animal, plant or other.<br /> <br /> The fact that at some point i sort of set-up a rough &quot;charm power scale chart&quot; would help me considerably with guesstimating the effectiveness of any such beings i threw in the PCs way.<br /> <br /> Everything gets much easier when you can roughly balance out the Exalt types among each other and against everybody else. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But overall i would do a lot out of getting already existing archetypes or even the occasional named NPC and using as a springboard for my own additions, customization and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-08-2024, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T07:41:00-08:00","id":1525345,"title":"","content":"Baaldam,<br /> <br /> I like your approach but don't toss hostile spirits at my players. It's not a fair fight when the PCs are a solar, a lunar, a sidereal, and three DBs who know Spirit-Shredding Attack.<br /> <br /> A couple months ago they tried to summon and bind Ligier. Ligier's response when he won the binding contest was to say &quot;Screw this, I'm outta here.&quot; and skeddale back to Malfeas ASAP because my NPCs aren't suicidal and I ain't gonna spend a few days giving an essence 10 spirt the full character sheet my players expect when I know what's about to happen to that spirit if it doesn't flee.<br /> <br /> When balancing enlightened mortals, terrestrials, and celestials I have a rule-of-thumb which seems to work: A terrestrial gets +100xp and an enlightened mortal gets +200xp","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T05:01:23-08:00","id":1525451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eumelia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525281-how-do-you-create-npcs?p=1525345#post1525345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baaldam,<br /> <br /> I like your approach but don't toss hostile spirits at my players. It's not a fair fight when the PCs are a solar, a lunar, a sidereal, and three DBs who know Spirit-Shredding Attack.<br /> <br /> A couple months ago they tried to summon and bind Ligier. Ligier's response when he won the binding contest was to say &quot;Screw this, I'm outta here.&quot; and skeddale back to Malfeas ASAP because my NPCs aren't suicidal and I ain't gonna spend a few days giving an essence 10 spirt the full character sheet my players expect when I know what's about to happen to that spirit if it doesn't flee.<br /> <br /> When balancing enlightened mortals, terrestrials, and celestials I have a rule-of-thumb which seems to work: A terrestrial gets +100xp and an enlightened mortal gets +200xp</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, that's where the &quot;power scale chart&quot; - that is inspired by the modifiers exalts get to wyld resistance rolls (pg.284 of the 2e core) comes in.<br /> Spirits &amp; God-Blooded - Essence<br /> Dragon-Blooded - Essence+1<br /> Sidereals, Lunars, Alchemicals - Essence+2<br /> Solars, Abyssals &amp; Green Sun Princes - Essence+3<br /> <br /> So, to sum it up, your average Ess 2 Solar charm would be roughly equivalent to an Ess3 sidereal or lunar charm, Essence 4 Dragon-Blooded charm or Essence 5 spirit charm, for example. With that in mind it becomes much simpler IMHO to balance and tweak a specific spirit's powerset - and yeah, i thought this up as something to help more with low to mid/high-tier antagonists, deities, demons, elementals &amp; ghosts in the Essence 2-6 range.<br /> <br /> Spirits with Essence 7+ are bonkers OP [Ligier with Ess7 solar charms?!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />] by that scheme, but since Essence 5-6 is when they get to access Celestial MA and/or Sorcery, they already were anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> (note that this is a <b>rough </b>equivalence, slightly bumping a charm's essence requirement up or down depending on the charm's themes and how well or badly would they fit a certain spirit or exalt type is completely fair)<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> Also, minions are a thing - Ligier is Essence 10 demon with &quot;legendary crafter&quot; on its themes. Next time your players pull a stunt like that, have a crafter, storm, demon shape a bunch of literal elementals of the appropriate type devoted to him into existence, Hosts of Spirits generating &quot;emanations of green light&quot; that empower/possess a number of mortals into Ess7 temporary god-bloods, or a variety of other tricks, for a little surprise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-15-2023, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T04:33:11-08:00","id":1525586,"title":"","content":"I generally don't stat NPCs unless I expect the PCs to fight or challenge them, and if they do then I try to have the least stat details for them that I can, often made up on the fly.<br /> <br /> Exalted demands enough from the GM as it is without statting every npc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T09:55:27-08:00","id":1525597,"title":"","content":"I often quickly decide what they'll be good at, and use the guide for what dots mean in the book. So a &quot;solidly competant mortal&quot; would throw like 6 dice on something they're good at. Mostly I just wing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T14:12:48-08:00","id":1525659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525281-how-do-you-create-npcs?p=1525597#post1525597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I often quickly decide what they'll be good at, and use the guide for what dots mean in the book. So a &quot;solidly competant mortal&quot; would throw like 6 dice on something they're good at. Mostly I just wing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My rule-of-thumb for an extra is &quot;4 dice if competence is expected, 1 die if it's not.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T15:56:28-08:00","id":1525756,"title":"","content":"My players decided to visit Ky\u014d. When I got to the quote part at the very end of Mizuki's description my wife started laughing while the teenagers looked at her in confusion.<br /> <br /> The quote: &quot;Do not mess with grandma for grandma has Exalted relatives and you are in her great house.&quot;<br /> <br /> My wife said &quot;What?&quot; before explaining that Mizuki is the local Dragon-Blooded Lord, a great-grandmother, and that there's an old joke in RPG circles: &quot;Do not meddle in the affairs of dragons for you are crunchy and taste good with ketchup.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mizuki's and description, from the NPC charsheet I created:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mizuki exalted in the remote far-eastern Scavanger Lands village of Ky\u014d. She is the illegitimate daughter of a Wood Aspect Dynast who passed through long ago and a local barmaid. All that's known about her father is a name: Cynis Sebas<br /> <br /> Almost immediately she became Lord of Ky\u014d.<br /> <br /> In addition to being the cordial hostess who owns Maple House, the local one-dot manse, inn, and tavern, Mizuki is a skilled archer and good hunter. It's a common occurance for the day's dinner special to be the wild boar she killed that morning.<br /> <br /> In Ky\u014d large families are desired and hers is no exception. In the century since her exaltation over twenty of her direct descendants have taken the second breath: ranging from her eldest daughter Ichiko (herself a nearly century-old Water Aspect and master of the Fire Dragon Style) to her 21-year old great-grandson Akito (an Exorcist and one of Ichiko's grandsons). Almost everyone who lives in Ky\u014d and the surrounding countryside - down to the lowliest farmhand - is tracebly related to Mizuki by blood or marriage.<br /> <br /> The local exaltation rate is quite high ... and rising. As such, the local school - founded by a retired and disillusioned Fire Immaculate Monk named Cathak N\u00edccolo after he retired to Maple House while Ichiko was a preteen - seeks to ensure universal literacy and offers classes in the Old Realm spoken by spirits on top of the Riverspeak and Forest-Tongue mortal <i>lingua francas</i> of the region. Tuition is free-and-public for the children of Ky\u014d.<br /> <br /> Mizuki has very good relations with Lookshy and there is always a Lookshy liason officer in Ky\u014d assisting the Ky\u014d Town Guard despite the distance. Ky\u014d produces silken armour and receives jade artifacts of comparable value in exchange.<br /> <br /> She does not have a high opinion of the Realm. When a representative of The Splendid and Just Arbiters of Purpose showed up to heavy-handedly and arrogantly reclaim the young &quot;Lost Egg&quot; that is Mizuki? She was out hunting and already Lord of Ky\u014d. He threatened her grandmother. He did not leave Ky\u014d alive. </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Edit: My players have been placed on notice: There are no extas in Ky\u014d and that the mortal chopping down a tree on the side of the road probably has occult:5 and knows Emerald Countermagic and Emerald Circle Banishment or, if he does not know those sorceries, is related to several someones who do know those sorceries.<br /> <br /> Burning Eyes of the Offender to screw an NPC's dicepools and Demon of the 1st Circle for slaves which get tossed into the meat grinder <i>won't work in Ky\u014d</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","user":"Eumelia","date":". 11-22-2023, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T09:15:10-08:00","id":1525844,"title":"","content":"I just figured out what my players want from Mizuki. Purity Crucible Strike from DoTFA.<br /> <br /> Mizuki is old enough to know that charm but would need to roll the dice and use it on herself <i>twice</i> before she uses it on the three DB PCs who want to raise their breeding background to five.<br /> <br /> Good luck with that. Mizuki has compassion 3 and isn't suicidal or power hungry. She knows both the charm and the risks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T07:29:12-08:00","id":1525876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eumelia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525281-how-do-you-create-npcs?p=1525844#post1525844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just figured out what my players want from Mizuki. Purity Crucible Strike from DoTFA.<br /> <br /> Mizuki is old enough to know that charm but would need to roll the dice and use it on herself <i>twice</i> before she uses it on the three DB PCs who want to raise their breeding background to five.<br /> <br /> Good luck with that. Mizuki has compassion 3 and isn't suicidal or power hungry. She knows both the charm and the risks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the fact Mizuki has breeding 3, something the three DB PCs should be able to notice if they just look at her with some attention, should be a pretty strong hint on itself that she either doesn't know the charm or doesn't care much for its use.\u200b<br /> <br /> (In fact, why does she have it in the first place?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T12:54:07-08:00","id":1525883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525281-how-do-you-create-npcs?p=1525876#post1525876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the fact Mizuki has breeding 3, something the three DB PCs should be able to notice if they just look at her with some attention, should be a pretty strong hint on itself that she either doesn't know the charm or doesn't care much for its use.\u200b<br /> <br /> (In fact, why does she have it in the first place?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I forgot to give her breeding 3 with BP when she Exalted. She needed that for Well-Tended Garden of the Soul.<br /> <br /> So, I sorta fudged things when she hit the century mark. That charm is also house-ruled to be presence 5, essence 5 with an age minimum thanks to another ST goof back when my players decided to pick a fight with the Perfect of Paragon. It's how they got rid of him, although the Dynast PC who used it was also one of the casualties.<br /> <br /> The PCs, in character, know about the charm. Mizuki is also an Outcaste elder with the breeding background. They're gonna figure she knows it so I may as well give them what they want.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T14:40:28-08:00","id":1525886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eumelia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525281-how-do-you-create-npcs?p=1525883#post1525883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I forgot to give her breeding 3 with BP when she Exalted. She needed that for Well-Tended Garden of the Soul.<br /> <br /> So, I sorta fudged things when she hit the century mark. That charm is also house-ruled to be presence 5, essence 5 with an age minimum thanks to another ST goof back when my players decided to pick a fight with the Perfect of Paragon. It's how they got rid of him, although the Dynast PC who used it was also one of the casualties.<br /> <br /> The PCs, in character, know about the charm. Mizuki is also an Outcaste elder with the breeding background. They're gonna figure she knows it so I may as well give them what they want.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that does explain things and that it makes sense equally from an IC perspective is a nice bonus.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, discussing charm vicissitudes reminds me of a &quot;elder Lunar killed thanks to Dog Tongue Method&quot; classic moment in a DotFA game long, long ago)<br /> <br /> That said, &quot;she's a DB elder, ergo she must have Purity Crucible Strike&quot; can be something of a jump. And Outcastes with Breeding definitely exist, as shown by Lookshy and other societies &amp; families of Shogunate remnants, not to mention illegitimate byblows of wandering high-breed Realm scions succeding at life and starting legacies of their own. Possible that they will find out it is, but there's much context (or meta knowledge) they need to see her as a strong candidate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-24-2023, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T16:07:23-08:00","id":1525888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525281-how-do-you-create-npcs?p=1525886#post1525886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, that does explain things and that it makes sense equally from an IC perspective is a nice bonus.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, discussing charm vicissitudes reminds me of a &quot;elder Lunar killed thanks to Dog Tongue Method&quot; classic moment in a DotFA game long, long ago)<br /> <br /> That said, &quot;she's a DB elder, ergo she must have Purity Crucible Strike&quot; can be something of a jump. And Outcastes with Breeding definitely exist, as shown by Lookshy and other societies &amp; families of Shogunate remnants, not to mention illegitimate byblows of wandering high-breed Realm scions succeding at life and starting legacies of their own. Possible that they will find out it is, but there's much context (or meta kn lolowledge) they need to see her as a strong candidate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured they'd would have picked Count Rik\u200b\u200b\u200bo and Havre as their next stop. He needs the most help, a Solar with Lore charms plus a Celestial with Raise The Puissant Sanctum can solve practically all of his Raksha problems and he would be more than happy to let the PCs keep<br /> about 2 dozen manses raised to his specs (He has blueprints).<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T17:11:53-08:00","id":1525891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525281-how-do-you-create-npcs?p=1525886#post1525886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(As an aside, discussing charm vicissitudes reminds me of a &quot;elder Lunar killed thanks to Dog Tongue Method&quot; classic moment in a DotFA game long, long ago)</div> </div> </div> </div>Another aside: My wife has lost an Adamant Circle Sorcerer to an angry extra with an axe because her PC did not have Ox-Body and got caught with his pants down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T18:08:17-08:00","id":1525987,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about this.<br /> <br /> Mizuki is about as immune to UMI as a 2E DB can get. Her dodge MDV is only 8 (good luck breaching that without charms or other magic) but Jade Defense and Inviolate Dragon Spirit pretty much renender her to immunne to UMI she isn't ok with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T21:40:28-08:00","id":1526264,"title":"","content":"My players tried to social-fu Mizuki. She did not acquiesce. It turned into a bar brawl which only the Lunar played by the younger of my daughters managed to escape.<br /> <br /> An enlightened mortal who knows Even Blade decapated my wife's essence 7 CMoS using Sidereal with one blow.\u200b<br /> <br /> EDIT: I had warned them that picking a fight with Mizuki was unwise. They decided to it despite me telling them that she, by herself, could go toe-to-toe with one Celestial PC and expect to win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","user":"Eumelia","date":". 12-03-2023, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T10:43:51-08:00","id":1526326,"title":"","content":"Since I'm sure <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> or others will be interested in how a circle of essence 4-7 Exalts nearly got TPKd in a bar brawl ...<br /> <br /> It was entirely their fault.<br /> <br /> When they got to town they were told to leave their weapons and armour with the Ky\u014d town guard, to be returned upon their departure. The Sid did not leave anything with the Ky\u014d town guard thinking they wouldn't spot the obvious martial artist and give everyone the heads up. That was mistake number one.<br /> <br /> Mistake two was one of the DBs using peripheral essence in Mizuki's tavern while talking to her. That's not polite and started the bar brawl.<br /> <br /> She rolled 17 successes on 25 dice for join battle while jumping over the bar to strangle the aforesaid DB. Everyone else present got stuck with tick 6 for their first action. I drew names out of a hat to unwind it because there were no extras present and the PCs were outnumbered 39:6 in a crowded room with no scene-lengths aside from All-Encompassing Earth Sense active.<br /> <br /> The Sid was stuck in a catch-22 because Avoidance Kata is neither Combo-OK nor Combo-Basic and he was gonna get a knife in the back with only 1L soak and one Ox-Body for protection from someone who was not an extra - at a bare minimum - when he used it on tick 6. The unexpected attack turned out to be something much worse: Deep Cut with a Reaper Daiklive.<br /> <br /> The Solar fared better. She was eating a bowl of soup when it started and used Melee Charms with a soup spoon. Dance of the Smoke Cobras killed her after the spoon broke when she used Heavenly Guardian Defense to parry the ceiling collapse.<br /> <br /> The Lunar fared the best by shapeshifting into a mouse. Still took 4bhl during &quot;Exit, Stage Left&quot; by way of getting accidently stepped on by several NPCs. An essence 6 Lunar with 26x(-2) health levels can ignore that.<br /> <br /> The three DBs were screwed from the get go. Unassailable Body of Earth Defense does nothing when the attacker knows Wood Dragon Elemental-Claw Strike and wants to strangle you. Portentious Comet Deflecting Mode? Working in that fustercluck? Wait, you're serious? Ok, let me laugh harder. Safety Among Enemies might work but you'll only get to use it once. Elemental Defense Technique and other scene lengths? Too late for that.<br /> <br /> The butchers bill: 5 dead, 1 wounded for the PCs. 9 dead, 29 wounded, and a damaged manse for the NPCs.<br /> <br /> The only character who wasn't killed or injured when the dust settled was the non-heroic waitress with valor 1 and wits 5. She dropped what she was carrying, fled to the manse's kitchen, and locked the door on her way out to once again keep the bar fight contained to the tavern part of the manse.<br /> <br /> In fairness though, Mizuki's use of Sweeten-the-Tap Method to make her tavern's booze better practically guaranteed a bar brawl involving essence wielders that she and her bouncers were expecting. Both bouncers were mortals which quite obviously had several dots of the Arsenel background. My players are also quite good at keeping OC and IC seperate so I let them access ST-eyes-only materials and generally don't resort to ST handwavium once the scene starts. OC, they knew what they were up against. IC, they carried out a Sidereal's Brilliant Plan and got slapped by destiny for their hubris.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28256-eumelia","name":"Eumelia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}